      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-07-22_WidnesExaminer_art0059" n="art0059">
        <head>EXAMINATION RESULTS.</head>
        <p>EXAMINATION RESULTS.</p>
        <p>The following children gave been awarded scholar- ships to the Preparatory Pupil Teachers' classes at the Secondary school for two years, to the value of five pounds per annum together with free tuition and the necessary books. The scholarships have been awarded upon the result of the examination recently held and the names are given in order of merit. viz :—Vera C. O'Brien William E. Wallington, Elsie N. Swaine, John M. Hopkins, May Hartree, Annie M. Roberts, Oswald White, May Baker, Ada Egerton, Wilfred M. Barton, Alice Bennie, Beatrice Dutton. _ _ . _ _</p>
        <p>The following childieri--Wh-o-did not obtain a suffi- ciently high position in the list to entitle them to scholarships to the Preparatory Pupil Teachers' classes have been awarded Free Studentships, for one year to those classes, viz :—Alice Taylor (Latchford), Mildred Ashley, Sybil Lister, Monica Vern On. Ada M. Baker, Kathleen E. Hankinsou, Alice Hough, Nellie R. Dunn, Thomas Stirrup, Stanley T. Morton, George H. Ellson. List of children who have qualified for admission to the Secondary school upon the result of the examination recently held, arranged in order of merit, viz Lily E. Simcock; 2, Elizabeth Appleton*; 3, Martha B. Wright; 4, Cyril R. Chambers; 5, William Allen, Dorothy Denham, Margaret Thomason*; 8, John M. Price; 9. Hilda Lister' 10, George A. Whit- field. Arthur Pemberton; 42, Robert G. Ormsby 13, Frank R. Wallington, Beatrice M. Wright*,Ralph H. Clatworthy ; 16, Rose D. Dell, Nora Brock, Annie Wilkinson, Stanley Rillington ; 20, Ethel M Brirnelow 21, Sydney Hyde; 22, Sarah Bracegirdle* ; 23, Edward H. Reddish; 24, Alfred Light; 25, Reginald J. H. Bell, Miriam Russell, Gladys Joynson; 28, John Sanders*; 29, George B Shepherd, Harold Partridge; ,131, Ellen Sudell* Frederick W. Wright ; 33, Florence Gordon; 34, Emily SI. Bowcock, Mary liackett* ; 36, Paterick H. Dorrian* ;37, Eierbert Eccles, Bessie Kay*, Violet M. Brown, Henry 13. Warburton ; 41, Rose Randall*,Florence Wainwright*, Elsie Hayes, Joseph L. Morton; 45 Thomas E. Smalley; 46, Edwin R. Hodg- son, Janet B. Oldroyd*, Elizabeth Acourt. *These children will, owing to the circumstances of their parents and on the recommendation of the Managers and Head Teachers of the Schools they attended, be admitted to the school free of charge.</p>
