        <p>Few people pause to reflect that this year is the twentieth anniversary of the birth of the Rover safety, which "set the fashion to the world." Many of us, including the writer, had been riding the high bicycle for years before. In a tent on the T ham es.Embankruent we first gazed upon the weird dwarf wheel destined to revolutionize the industry and the pastime. The triumph of .the safety was not achieved in a season; indeed, it took the best part of five years before the number of its riders became numerically conspicuous. Not a few.orcli- naryists descended from their lofty seats through , the lowlier geared ordinary and the still lowlier front driver to the safety, taking ten years in the Process. But those of us who still ride are all •••••4 nrn,oininlAr onrtn,^l,,,l tri'fb</p>
